menu "CYB3RGUN camera bench"

config CGCAM_CLOCK_HZ
    int "SPI clock in Hz"
    range 100000 14000000
    default 1000000
    help
        The part does 14 MHz on a board, but its pins drive 4 mA into a
        specified 100 pF, so flying wires get 1 to 2 MHz. concept.md
        section 5.

config CGCAM_SPI_MODE
    int "SPI mode"
    range 0 3
    default 3
    help
        The bus timing section of the datasheet is past the end of the copy
        in THEHARDWARE, so this is a value to try rather than a value that
        is known. If the probe finds nothing, try the other three. D-012.

config CGCAM_PROBE_BANKS
    int "How many register banks the probe sweeps"
    range 1 32
    default 16
    help
        1 stays on whatever bank the module powers up in and needs no write
        at all, which is the safest first attempt. More than 1 writes the
        bank register before each sweep.

config CGCAM_DUMP_REG
    int "First register of the window the bench reads each frame"
    range 0 255
    default 0
    help
        Once the output access map of datasheet section 7.4 is in hand, this
        is where the object data starts.

config CGCAM_DUMP_LEN
    int "How many bytes the bench reads each frame"
    range 1 256
    default 32

config CGCAM_FPS
    int "Frames per second the bench reads at"
    range 1 200
    default 50
    help
        S01-B01 task 5 asks for 50. The part itself does up to 200.

endmenu
